THOUGHT: The build output still shows NullAway errors but not the original one, so my previous edit likely didn’t apply correctly. I need to safely guard the nullable taskExecutor in shutdown() with a null check, then rebuild to confirm the specific error is gone and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/eureka && sed -i '112,118c\  public void shutdown() {
    ScheduledExecutorService localTaskExecutor = taskExecutor;
    if (localTaskExecutor != null) {
      localTaskExecutor.shutdown();
    }
    List<PeerEurekaNode> toRemove = this.peerEurekaNodes;

    this.peerEurekaNodes = Collections.emptyList();
    this.peerEurekaNodeUrls = Collections.emptySet();

    for (PeerEurekaNode node : toRemove) {
      node.shutDown();
    }
  }' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/cluster/PeerEurekaNodes.java && ./gradlew eureka-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "PeerEurekaNodes" new_build_output.log || sed -n '108,125p' eureka-core/src/main/java/com/netflix/eureka/cluster/PeerEurekaNodes.java
```

